  "note": "Triennial election, polled Monday 15 May 1939; nineteen candidates for fifteen seats over the whole town. 4,071 votes cast, 32 spoilt. \"Messrs Greenaway and Flanigan are Roman Catholics. This is the first time for many years that two Roman Catholics have been elected in Portadown.\" Party labels are not printed. The last Portadown election before the wartime postponement; the next was in September 1946."
